# Current resource-partition scope, source-only reconfirmation

The existing `performance/PERFORMANCE-AUDIT.md` already records why the current recipe is ineligible for stream quotas. This follow-up does not add a hardware experiment or acceptance gate.

Pinned Ascend `03766ac696fde5ab1980d80ca0b8543d3580c989`, `vllm_ascend/worker/model_runner_v1.py:207`, explicitly sets `torch.npu.config.allow_internal_format = True`. The qualified runs use that V1 runner. This is a source/configuration finding; no new live-worker RPC or device-format measurement was performed during the frozen quality run.

The official [TorchNPU stream-limit contract](https://www.hiascend.com/document/detail/en/Pytorch/2610/apiref/customapi/docs/en/custom_APIs/torch_npu/torch_npu-set_stream_limit.md) requires internal formats to be disabled and restricts supported operators. Its current official search-index entry was rechecked on 2026-10-26; direct page retrieval timed out. The older 7.3 documentation URL currently returned the website shell in this read, so the 26.1 official link is a useful additional navigation target. The installed Python API is present at `/usr/local/python3.12.13/lib/python3.12/site-packages/torch_npu/npu/npu_config.py:259`; it invokes the native stream-resource setter, which does not itself establish compatibility of model operators.

Therefore stream quotas remain disabled for this unchanged recipe. The current implementation's separate P/D execution and latency observations are not a claim of the paper's Cube/Vector spatial partitioning. This does not rule out a future distinct configuration with private formats disabled and the necessary operator/graph validation. No quota, format, model, source or running process was changed by this check.

For final documentation, retain this bounded limitation and link the existing audit. Update historical pending language separately from the original audit snapshot; do not require an exhaustive operator qualification for a recipe already excluded by the documented format precondition.
